## Ratified 2026-08-31 — the proposal is the chain's now

R29 entered the sheet on the author's ruling, amended in three places; the
ruling and its amendments are in `spec/DECISIONS.md`. Nothing in this ticket is
authoritative any more. Where each part of the former proposal now lives:

| what | owner |
|---|---|
| R29 itself, and query translation being out of scope | `spec/REQUIREMENTS.md` |
| the ruling, and the amendments to the proposal as drafted | `spec/DECISIONS.md` |
| the mechanism -- the embedding space as the only cross-lingual channel, the fusion seam, the typed degradation disclosure | `spec/DESIGN.md` 2.6 |
| the cross-lingual slice of the golden gate, separately gated | `spec/DESIGN.md` 2.8; ticket 0029 builds it and pins its thresholds |
| R29 as a conformance criterion in the embedder ship gate | ticket 0495 |
| the measurement, per language pair and per deployed dtype, with both controls | ticket 0266, `bench/results/0266-cross-lingual/` |
| where each requirement stands, R29 included | `spec/README.md` |

The proposal's "new experiment X8" was not carried. The label had since been
taken by cross-provider fidelity (`spec/DESIGN.md` 3), and ticket 0266 had
already run the measurement it asked for, so no experiment label was allocated
and the design cites the evidence instead. The proposal's CONSTRAINTS.md
sharpenings were not carried there either: they are facts about the two query
paths, so they landed with their owner in `spec/DESIGN.md` 2.6.

## Exit criteria
- [x] Proposal put to the author; the ruling lands in DECISIONS.md
- [x] REQUIREMENTS.md gains R29 and the out-of-scope sentence; DESIGN.md 2.6
      and 2.8 gain the amendments; this body becomes pointers
- [x] No experiment label allocated -- amended away, the measurement existed
- [x] 0029's scope extended with the cross-lingual slice
